## std/reader — the Reader<R> algebraic effect.
##
## Operation Piezoelectric Effects, Phase 2, Milestone P2.b.
##
## `Reader` is a read-only ambient-value effect: callers inside a
## `with Reader(v) do ... end` block can `ask()` to retrieve `v`. Nested
## `with Reader(...)` blocks get their own independent slot — inner shadows
## outer, outer is unchanged on scope exit. Implementation reuses the
## evidence-slot machinery from P2.a (`State<S>`); the only difference is
## the default handler's dispatch table (`ask` vs. `get`/`set`).
##
## Usage:
##
##   import std/reader
##
##   def greet() can Reader = "hello, " + as_string(ask())
##
##   def main(): Int
##     puts(with Reader(as_int("world")) do -> greet() end)
##     return 0
##   end
##
## Shadowing via `local`: within a Reader scope, run `body` against a
## transformed version of the current value. Equivalent to an inline
## `with Reader(f(ask())) do -> body() end` — but `local` is polymorphic
## over the effect row of `body`, so callers composing Reader with other
## effects (Throws, Log, State) don't have to rewrite the row. `local`
## requires the caller to already be in a Reader scope (it reads the
## current value via `ask()`).
##
##   with Reader(10) do ->
##     local(x -> x + 1, () -> ask())  # returns 11 — inner shadow
##     ask()                           # returns 10 — outer unchanged
##   end
##
## Type-parameter note: `Reader<R>` parses but `<R>` erases at runtime —
## every value is i64-sized. `Reader<Config>` stores the config pointer as
## i64; `ask()`'s return value is recovered via `as_string` / cast.

effect Reader
  def ask(): Int
end

## Run `body` under a Reader scope whose ambient value is `f(ask())`.
## The outer Reader's value is restored when `body` returns. `f` maps
## the current ambient to a new ambient for `body` to observe.
##
## `body`'s effect row is `can Reader | r` (row-polymorphic tail `r`) so
## callers composing Reader with other effects pass through transparently.
## P2.b MVP fixes the tail to just `Reader`; row-polymorphic `local` is
## a P3.F-style followup once trait/row plumbing stabilizes.
def local(f: Fn(Int): Int, body: Fn(): Int): Int can Reader
  var current = ask()
  var shadowed = f(current)
  return with Reader(shadowed) do -> body() end
end
